{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1167534-specialties-in-untrained-skills","id":1167534,"title":"Specialties in untrained Skills","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-13T23:35:10-08:00","id":1167534,"title":"Specialties in untrained Skills","content":"Hi guys, first time on these forums and fairly new to CoD but I'm already playing Mage after a bit of Beast, solid and engaging RPGs to say the least. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Since I started I've been told by my ST that Specialties can't be assigned to untrained Skills; this always bugged me, as I never saw that written anywhere (besides, IRL I have had a first aid training while having no other knowledges concerning medicine). I trust my ST, he's been very accommodating, but when I delv into a rule system I want to master it and achieve an encyclopedic comprehension of it. So...<br /> <br /> 1. Can anybody point me to a specific piece of text that addresses the matter?<br /> 2. If no such text exists, would assigning Specs to such Skills be unreasonable?<br /> 2a. Would such a Specialty incur in the Untrained penalty?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance! (^^)/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23578-shinkiro","name":"Shinkiro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T03:46:48-08:00","id":1167561,"title":"","content":"1) Not really, between all the books it has been stated a few times, but it is generally not. In 1e it was clarified on the forums that the intent was for Specialties to require a Skill dot first, but enough people seem to like the option that it wouldn't be the first time the developers left someone vague so people can run it either way.<br /> <br /> 2) I'm not sure it's unreasonable, but it is problematic. This mostly because the RAW answer to 2a would be that Untrained penalties still apply, as they apply if you have no dots in a Skill, and a Specialty isn't a dot in a Skill. Allowing people to apply Specialties to untrained Skills is basically a mechanical trap. You're always better off buying the first dot of the Skill, so letting people take a suboptimal option shouldn't really be encouraged.<br /> <br /> As to the more general point, the Skills in the CofD are very broad. It's just the level of abstraction and granularity that the system goes for. The game isn't trying to model real life, so the minimum competence for 1 dot in a Skill being a bit higher than might feel right is an acceptable break from reality to avoid a much more cumbersome Skill system. I also think people have a tendency to underestimate the amount of general knowledge that gets picked up in training and life experiences. I'm pretty sure that even if you've never had medical training beyond first aid, you actually have medical knowledge beyond first aid techniques. Most people with at least the equivalent of a Western highschool education have a basic knowledge base of things like anatomy, germ theory, hygiene, pharmacology, nutrition, and so on. <br /> <br /> It's also worth looking a bit at the mechanical side. 1 dot in a Skill just... isn't a lot. For something like Medicine, you're frequently looking at extended actions, and you only get (Attribute + Skill) rolls for those. So if you're doing first-aid beyond stabilizing a patient out in the field, with Dexterity 3 and Medicine 1, you only get to roll four times. If the injuries are too severe (6+ damage) you're odds of helping are minimal, and for moderate wounds where you're going to be rolling most of your rolls, there's good odds you inflict a negative Condition on your patient even if you reduce their damage a bit (or you just opt to fail instead of doing that). Taking a 1 in a Skill isn't going to realistically turn a character into someone that's overly competent, because hard things have ways to being hard on you for trying them when you're only a novice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T11:41:57-08:00","id":1167725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1167534-specialties-in-untrained-skills?p=1167561#post1167561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most people with at least the equivalent of a Western highschool education have a basic knowledge base of things like anatomy, germ theory, hygiene, pharmacology, nutrition, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact you remind me, if I'm not wrong, that the value of dots in everything, from Skills to Equipment, is contestualized in the Chronicle: in Tokyo the value in dots of a gun skyrockets while in Detroit's downtown may be common place to have a gun instead of, say, a smartphone.<br /> <br /> I thought it could have been a leftover of 1e, my ST has a whole history in WoD, and now I have proof. Fine to me, I agree the game doesn't need extra convolution.<br /> <br /> Thanks again for the fast answer!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23578-shinkiro","name":"Shinkiro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T13:53:31-08:00","id":1167764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinkiro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1167534-specialties-in-untrained-skills?p=1167725#post1167725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In fact you remind me, if I'm not wrong, that the value of dots in everything, from Skills to Equipment, is contestualized in the Chronicle: in Tokyo the value in dots of a gun skyrockets while in Detroit's downtown may be common place to have a gun instead of, say, a smartphone.<br /> <br /> I thought it could have been a leftover of 1e, my ST has a whole history in WoD, and now I have proof. Fine to me, I agree the game doesn't need extra convolution.<br /> <br /> Thanks again for the fast answer!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe the fluctuating value of &quot;Equipment&quot; relates to services and equipment costs, as far as scarcity is concerned.<br /> <br /> I could be wrong, but my impression from the reading of Chronicles of Darkness and Mage corebooks was that Skill dots mean the same thing across the globe, no matter what region you're in - hence, why they go so far as to distinguish you as world-class. There would be no point in distinguishing you as world-class if that classification meant something different in New York vs Antarctica.<br /> <br /> The value of a gun increasing in Tokyo would just be a by-product of them not having 300 million guns hanging around like in the USA, as well as their extremely strict gun laws.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Western highschool education&quot; bit is to highlight how convoluted real life can be (regarding the things you know about either directly or indirectly). World of Darkness isn't trying to mimic that level of complexity, where someone with no formal training still knows the basics of First Aid from watching TV, movies, a youtube video, or passing by a Heimlich poster.<br /> <br /> As stated before, a specialty isn't a dot, and using a skill without dots invokes a penalty. It seems like you'd be playing with adding more balancing of numbers because you'd be trying to juggle penalties against bonuses that likely leave you with negative modifier on the rolls to start with.<br /> <br /> I mean, if that's the kind of game you're trying to play with your ST, all the power to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T14:09:58-08:00","id":1167768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinkiro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1167534-specialties-in-untrained-skills?p=1167725#post1167725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact you remind me, if I'm not wrong, that the value of dots in everything, from Skills to Equipment, is contestualized in the Chronicle: in Tokyo the value in dots of a gun skyrockets while in Detroit's downtown may be common place to have a gun instead of, say, a smartphone.<br /> <br /> I thought it could have been a leftover of 1e, my ST has a whole history in WoD, and now I have proof. Fine to me, I agree the game doesn't need extra convolution.<br /> <br /> Thanks again for the fast answer!</div> </div> </div> </div>As noted by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11166\" data-vbnamecard=\"11166\">kryptonitekrusher</a> the values for most Traits isn't actually supposed to be contextualized.<br /> <br /> Resources is explicitly contextualized because it represents spare money rather than some sort of absolute value. My current income where I live is enough for me to have Resources 2 or 3 in CofD mechanics, because the cost of living here is very low by US standards. If I moved to a major city, I'd easily drop to Resource 0 simply because of the increased cost in living, and Sanctity of Merits something something 2 spare Merit dots.<br /> <br /> This then plays into Availability and equipment by necessity of Resources being contextual.<br /> <br /> However the game expects Academics 1 to cover the approximate same level of education across the globe. The way the game expects you to contextualize this is with situational modifiers. A person that grew up in Germany might get a +1 or +2 situational bonus due to familiarity for an Academics check relating to German history, where someone that studied in the US might have a -1 or -2 penalty on the same check because the US education system doesn't cover much of German history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T15:47:04-08:00","id":1167785,"title":"","content":"People used to some other systems sometimes find it difficult to grasp what a single dot means in CoD. Your 1st Aid training, by the way, would probably be represented as a first dot in Medicine, not as a Specialty in 1st Aid. Someone with both a dot and a specialty would already be a technician, able to work on a daily basis with this, though still following instructions. A person truly with a Specialty but without a single dot would be, even if without the Untrained penalty, someone extremely focused and limited, trained at exhaustion in a task but unable to develop understanding from there.<br /> <br /> In the 1st Aid example, it would be someone who memorized perfectly a set of instructions, but couldn't comprehend how its components cause any change to the patient. If the problem is outside of this precise set of instructions, this person will be lost. It does happen in real life, and is relatively common, but most of the time it isn't enough to warrant the space in your character sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}